Date: 18 Nov 1980 (Tuesday) 2034-EDT
From: OTTO at WHARTON (George Otto)
Subject: Info about Parallel Processors Wanted
To:   setnet at MIT-AI

I am interested in what research is being done currently with large sets
of small parallel-processing computers which have the following properties:
  
  * Each computer can run its own program with its own modest memory
    (1-4Kbytes?)
  * Each computer is ostensibly independent of the rest, but can
    be "acquired" by another to run subtasks
  * Each computer can send messages to any other computer in the set
    with low efficiency   
  * Each computer can send messages to selected other computers in the  
    set with high efficiency (dynamic establishment of priority links?)

How many computers are currently being sonsidered in suts under development
right now? Where are they being developed?
 
