HAL@MIT-MC 07/20/80 21:52:31
To: setnet at MIT-AI

danny--

i looked over QBE.  I don't exactly understand it, but i also think it
isn't right and breaks down when there is more than one variable.

suppose we have two relations -- (R1 (ATT-a ATT-b)) and
(R2 (ATT-c ATT-d))

suppose we query on the pair of patterns:

(R1 (ATT-a x?) (ATT-b y?))
(R2 (ATT-c x?) (ATT-d y?))

Then won't your algorithm end up with extra entries?

For example, if the data base is

(R1 (ATT-a 1) (ATT-b 2))
(R2 (ATT-a 1) (ATT-b 6))
(R2 (ATT-a 5) (ATT-b 2))

Then the algorithm will check the first pattern and find that 1 and 5
are good values for ATT-a, then will check the 2nd pattern and find
that 2 and 6 are good values for ATT-b.

Then it will check all the tuples and decide that all of them match
the pattern.

Or am I missing something?


